  type: 1
  description: 123
  title: Basic Data Movement
  content: "Lesson 1: Basic Data Movement\r\nObjective: Understand how to transfer
    data between registers, memory, and the stack.\r\nInstructions Covered:\r\n\r\nMOV:
    Moves data between registers or between memory and registers.\r\nMOV AX, BX    
    ; AX gets the value in BX\r\nMOV AL, 5      ; AL gets the value 5\n\nPUSH and
    POP: Push data onto the stack and pop it back.\r\nPUSH AX        ; Saves AX on
    the stack\r\nPOP AX         ; Retrieves the last value pushed into AX\n\nExercise
    Application: You\u2019ll use MOV to set values in registers and PUSH/POP for
    managing values on the stack in Exercise 3 (Stack Spider)."
